api_examples:
Example streaming frames (JSONL lines) sent over an open SSE/websocket socket:

{"frame_id":"f-1","seq":1,"type":"delta_text","text":"Drafting summary: The Q4 invoice reconciliation shows a 12% discrepancy..."}
{"frame_id":"f-2","seq":2,"type":"assertion","assertions":[{"label":"entities:invoice","confidence":0.93,"schema":"/schemas/invoice-v2","actionability":"optimistic"}]}
{"frame_id":"f-3","seq":3,"type":"tool_hint","tool":{"id":"extract-invoice","version":"v1","reason":"high-confidence invoice entity"}}
{"frame_id":"f-4","seq":4,"type":"commit","status":"final"}

Notes: - 'actionability' can be 'optimistic'|'conservative'|'must_confirm'. - Clients decide whether to call 'extract-invoice' on receiving frame f-3 depending on configured thresholds and current network profile. - Frames are retriable and carry 'frame_id' for idempotency.
